<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06VC">Example <span data-tag="06VC">9.5.6.18</span> <span class="named">(Truncated Objects)</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a presentable $\infty $-category, let $n$ be an integer, and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\leq n}$ denote the full subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ spanned by the $n$-truncated objects. Then $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\leq n}$ is a Bousfield localization of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. This is a special case of Proposition <a data-tag="06V9" href="/tag/06V9">9.5.6.15</a>, since the full subcategory $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\leq n}$ is accessibly embedded (Corollary <a data-tag="06UC" href="/tag/06UC">9.4.9.14</a>) and closed under limits (Corollary <a data-tag="06TJ" href="/tag/06TJ">7.3.8.7</a>). </p>
</article>
